{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/674894-seasonal-courts-in-changeling","id":674894,"title":"Seasonal Courts in Changeling?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-22T20:46:02-07:00","id":674894,"title":"Seasonal Courts in Changeling?","content":"I keep seeing people mention seasonal courts in <i>Changeling: the Dreaming</i> . .something I don't remember at all. There was the Seelie court of Concordia, under High King David, and the revolutionary (and very Unseelie) Shadow Court. That was it. <br /> <br /> However, I never picked up second edition. Can anyone catch me up? When did we get a court of Spring/Summer/Fall/Winter? And are they political entities? Or something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T23:03:41-07:00","id":674952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/674894-seasonal-courts-in-changeling#post674894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep seeing people mention seasonal courts in <i>Changeling: the Dreaming</i> . .something I don't remember at all. There was the Seelie court of Concordia, under High King David, and the revolutionary (and very Unseelie) Shadow Court. That was it.<br /> <br /> However, I never picked up second edition. Can anyone catch me up? When did we get a court of Spring/Summer/Fall/Winter? And are they political entities? Or something else?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There were seasonal courts in DA FAE and there's some symbolic connection between seelie and Unseelie and the seasons but that's it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T06:45:56-07:00","id":675190,"title":"","content":"There's also that the courts would each switch rulership for half the year - seelie in the spring and summer, unseelie in the fall and winter. In more recent years, though, the cycle has been disrupted. Now whichever court gains power tends to keep it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T12:04:49-07:00","id":675576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/674894-seasonal-courts-in-changeling#post674894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep seeing people mention seasonal courts in <i>Changeling: the Dreaming</i> . .something I don't remember at all. There was the Seelie court of Concordia, under High King David, and the revolutionary (and very Unseelie) Shadow Court. That was it.<br /> <br /> However, I never picked up second edition. Can anyone catch me up? When did we get a court of Spring/Summer/Fall/Winter? And are they political entities? Or something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure you aren't thinking of <b>Changeling: The Lost</b>? As mentioned above, <b>Dark Ages: Fae</b> does include seasonal courts as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T23:45:09-07:00","id":676104,"title":"","content":"in fairness there is a lot of seasonal symbolism in C:tD. Autumn and winter are associated with banality/nightmares spring and summer with dreams/glamour. For example, the material world is often called 'The Autumn World' and the 'The Autumn People' are often another name for Dautain. Likewise the Shadow Court hopes to rule the world through the Endless Winter. But no there is no specific seasonal courts in the style of Dark Ages: Fae or Changeling the Lost that I've come across.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T05:10:13-07:00","id":680902,"title":"","content":"Maybe if we ever get a Guide to the Seelie and a Guide to the Unseelie, they might break down individual personality types and factions in each court in such a way that we learn how the seasonal courts developed into the modern ones, but there isn't anything else outside of DA: Fae, really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}